  "body": {
    "id": "prop:centrosymmetric-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "The actual compact-polyhedral overlap with Theorem 4 of \\cite{MontielOleaQiuStoye2026Local} is a proper subclass of the proposed two-dimensional regime:\n\\[\n\\mathcal O_2^{(4)}\\subsetneq\\mathcal G_2.\n\\]\nThe inclusion follows from \\(\\mathcal O_2^{(4)}\\subseteq\\mathcal G_2^{\\mathrm{cs}}\\subseteq\\mathcal G_2\\), while strictness is certified by the triangular game in \\(\\mathrm{prop:coexistence-witness}\\), which belongs to \\(\\mathcal G_2\\) but not to \\(\\mathcal G_2^{\\mathrm{cs}}\\), and hence not to \\(\\mathcal O_2^{(4)}\\). Thus \\(\\mathrm{thm:complete-saddle-duality}\\) applies both to every game in the compact-polyhedral overlap and to at least one asymmetric game outside that overlap. No inclusion between \\(\\mathcal G_p\\) and the full published Assumption-5 class is asserted.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(\\mathsf G\\)",
      "\\(p\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal G_p^{\\mathrm{cs}}\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal O_p^{(4)}\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal G_p\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:centrosymmetric-comparator-class",
      "def:theorem4-overlap",
      "thm:complete-saddle-duality",
      "prop:coexistence-witness",
      "def:coexistence-witness"
    ],
    "justification": "The proposition proves the only strict-extension statement used in the proposal: the new two-dimensional class strictly contains the actual compact-polyhedral Theorem 4 overlap, with strictness supplied by an explicit asymmetric game.",
    "gap": "Assumption 5 with Theorem 4 of \\cite{MontielOleaQiuStoye2026Local} covers a directionally differentiable centrosymmetric class. This proposition compares only on the defined compact-polyhedral overlap and does not claim that the proposed class contains the full published Assumption-5 class.",
    "consumer": "Researchers can identify exactly when the published centered solver is in scope and when the asymmetric all-saddle analysis supplies genuinely additional admissible games.",
    "proof_tex": "By \\(\\mathrm{def:theorem4-overlap}\\), every element of \\(\\mathcal O_2^{(4)}\\) is an element of \\(\\mathcal G_2^{\\mathrm{cs}}\\), and by \\(\\mathrm{def:centrosymmetric-comparator-class}\\), every element of \\(\\mathcal G_2^{\\mathrm{cs}}\\) is an element of \\(\\mathcal G_2\\). Hence\n\\[\n \\mathcal O_2^{(4)}\\subseteq\\mathcal G_2^{\\mathrm{cs}}\\subseteq\\mathcal G_2. \\tag{1}\n\\]\nThe game in \\(\\mathrm{def:coexistence-witness}\\) belongs to \\(\\mathcal G_2\\) by \\(\\mathrm{prop:coexistence-witness}\\), whereas its triangular domain satisfies \\(H_0\\neq-H_0\\), so it does not belong to \\(\\mathcal G_2^{\\mathrm{cs}}\\). By (1) it cannot belong to \\(\\mathcal O_2^{(4)}\\). Thus the first inclusion into \\(\\mathcal G_2\\) is proper. Application of \\(\\mathrm{thm:complete-saddle-duality}\\) to every member of \\(\\mathcal G_2\\) then covers both every game in \\(\\mathcal O_2^{(4)}\\) and this explicit asymmetric game. The proof compares only the two sets in (1), so it entails no relation between \\(\\mathcal G_p\\) and the full published Assumption-5 class.",
